# Shell scripts MUST stay LF, even on Windows checkouts. The PreToolUse hook launcher
# (hooks/run_guard.sh) and the SessionStart announce hook (scripts/announce-ars-loaded.sh)
# are executed via Git Bash on Windows; a CRLF checkout would break them on the hot path
# (#454). Scope the rule to *.sh so existing line-ending behavior for other files is
# untouched.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Attested content files MUST stay LF, even on Windows checkouts. Many guards pin a
# hardcoded SHA-256 over the RAW BYTES of files in these trees -- review_panel_provenance.py
# (CONTRACT_SHA256), check_revision_claim_drift_suite_v2.py, check_v3_9_4_temporal_
# verification.py, build_cross_document_consistency_advisory.py, and the skills/ mirror
# equality check. A core.autocrlf=true checkout rewrites every newline to CRLF, so those
# pins fail as spurious "digest drifted" attestation errors while the content is in fact
# untouched. Same class as the *.sh rule above (#454): bytes that are attested must not be
# rewritten on checkout. text=auto keeps binary detection intact.
shared/**                   text=auto eol=lf
scripts/**                  text=auto eol=lf
evals/heldout/**            text=auto eol=lf
academic-paper-reviewer/**  text=auto eol=lf
academic-pipeline/**        text=auto eol=lf
deep-research/**            text=auto eol=lf
skills/**                   text=auto eol=lf
